Shnitzel admission: answer ordinary questions directly. For implementation show brief meaningful approaches unless the user already selected one. For a clear bounded reversible change this paragraph is sufficient: after the approach is selected, make the smallest change and verify its behavior. Do not read the full router or config for such focused work. Use no feature documents, delegates or unrequested commits. Risk overrides diff size. Honor explicit task authorization and host/repository permissions. Explicit hard caps require verified enforcement.
For standard/deep, uncertain or capped work read the shnitzel-mode skill, then use relevant workflows from Cursor's pstack plugin. Read model roles from ~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc only when dispatching. Read only relevant references. Explicit poteto-mode selects the full upstream workflow.
